{
  "what": "The door history of an element: doorsOf (npm SDK) and doors_of (Python package) on the same cases, and doorWhere and door_where on each entry they give. Every expected list is written by hand. The same bytes in both packages; each test holds this file's sha256.",
  "keys": "tools is the tools list every case reads, unless the case carries its own tools. element is an element body as the API serves it (doors, changed_client, changed_via, updated_at). expected is the entries in order, each {door, at, tool, last, from}, tool null or the matched row's {id, name}. where is the phrase doorWhere and door_where give for each expected entry, in the same order.",
  "tools": [
    {
      "id": "atlas",
      "name": "Atlas",
      "url": "https://atlas.example",
      "client": "atlas",
      "rung": "listed",
      "open": null
    },
    {
      "id": "atlas-beta",
      "name": "Atlas Beta",
      "url": "https://beta.atlas.example",
      "client": "atlas",
      "rung": "built",
      "open": null
    },
    {
      "id": "lantern",
      "name": "Lantern",
      "url": "https://lantern.example",
      "client": "lantern",
      "rung": "listed",
      "open": null
    },
    {
      "id": "corvid",
      "name": "Corvid",
      "url": "https://corvid.example",
      "client": null,
      "rung": "listed",
      "open": null
    }
  ],
